WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.580
In under two minutes, you will add a sponsor and its logo to your contest.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:05.694
We start on the map.

00:00:06.597 --> 00:00:09.987
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.998 --> 00:00:14.439
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:14.439 --> 00:00:16.947
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.947 --> 00:00:18.303
Tap Use my location.

00:00:20.112 --> 00:00:22.435
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:22.435 --> 00:00:23.119
Tap Allow.

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:28.430
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:29.555
See the three dots?

00:00:29.555 --> 00:00:30.061
Tap them.

00:00:32.204 --> 00:00:34.038
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:36.385
Tap Mine.

00:00:36.385 --> 00:00:38.246
These are the contests you run.

00:00:39.926 --> 00:00:41.976
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:41.976 --> 00:00:43.363
This is your dashboard.

00:00:45.272 --> 00:00:46.654
Tap Sponsors.

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:51.174
Type the sponsor's name, and choose a tier.

00:00:53.463 --> 00:00:55.959
Add their website, and choose their logo.

00:00:59.318 --> 00:01:00.385
Tap Add sponsor.

00:01:00.385 --> 00:01:04.531
Sponsors can pay you directly, and payment never affects who wins.

00:01:06.462 --> 00:01:09.237
To check how it looks, tap See it as voters do.

00:01:11.253 --> 00:01:14.503
Next up: Presenting installer and quote requests.
